<title>UK: ABF falls as Hoare Govett cuts forecasts.</title>
<headline>ABF falls as Hoare Govett cuts forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Associated British Foods Plc dropped on Tuesday as analysts at ABN Amro Hoare Govett cut profit forecasts due to the recent appreciation in sterling.</p>
<p>Shares in AB Foods were down 9-1/2p at 476p by 1040 GMT.</p>
<p>A spokesman for Hoare Govett said current year forecasts were cut by 15 million stg. Analysts at the brokerage were previously expecting pre-tax profits to reach 413 million stg.</p>
<p>Hoare Govett maintains a &quot;hold&quot; recommendation on the stock.</p>
<p>-- Paul Carrel, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
